// The curated catalog of known trophies (issue #342).
//
// Source: BBL's own authoritative trophy legend pages, `default.asp?p=tt`
// (team trophies) and `default.asp?p=ppr` (player trophies) -- confirmed
// exhaustive at 16 + 12 = 28 entries, matching every distinct `gfx/prizeN.gif`
// icon found anywhere in the mirrored BBL dataset. Descriptions are
// translated from the original Swedish. Four further trophies (Ogretoberfest
// and the three Dungeon Bowl placements) are TP-only and have no BBL
// equivalent.
//
// Trophies deliberately carry NO shared "Name" external id, the same
// precedent competitions set in issue #285: superficially identical labels
// (e.g. "1st") can be genuinely different trophies depending on the
// competition tier, so identity is a curation decision, never inferred from
// label text. BBL's *team* trophy labels ARE self-disambiguating (`Major 1st`
// vs. `Minor 1st`), so each of those is keyed by the exact BBL label text
// itself (matching the raw source id/label convention every other
// curated-data file and every real BBL importer use -- no prefix).
//
// BBL's *player* trophy labels are NOT self-disambiguating (issue #520): BBL
// hands the same "Deadliest Player" or "Legendary Player" label out in
// several competition groups, so the label alone identifies no single
// trophy. Every such trophy/group combination confirmed in the cached BBL
// data therefore gets its own row, keyed `${label}-${groupName}` -- the same
// hyphen-joined composite the tourplay.net ids below use. The original Major
// Season rows keep their bare-label ids unchanged, so a Major-Season award
// still resolves exactly as before, and BblTrophyAwardsImportService tries
// the composite key first and falls back to the bare label. 12 such composite
// rows exist: 7 Minor Season variants of the "during the season" player
// trophies, 3 Legendary Player groups (Chaos Cup, Ogretoberfest, Champion of
// tLoEG) and 2 Trogen Tjänst groups (Moot Mania, Chaos Cup). "Season MVP"
// deliberately has none -- no cross-group award of it is confirmed in the
// cached data, and the server-side group-match check would surface one
// loudly if it ever appeared.
//
// TP external ids (issue #446) are seeded for the 10 trophies TP actually
// awards, keyed as `${disambiguator}-${groupName}` -- the same hyphen-joined
// composite BBL positions use (`${typId}-${race.bblId}`). TP's raw
// `awardType` codes (1/2/3, 100/200) are NOT globally unique per trophy: the
// same code means a different trophy depending on which competition tier it
// appears in, so the competition group's name (issue #445) is what scopes it.
// The disambiguator is the raw award's `name` field when present ("Best
// Stunty", "Wooden Spoon" -- which share one numeric awardType within a file,
// so the name is the only thing that separates them) and the numeric
// `awardType` otherwise (1/2/3).
//
// 10 entries are seeded, confirmed by reading all 13 local TP award files: TP
// has so far only tracked 4 competition groups (Major Season, Chaos Cup,
// Dungeon Bowl, Ogretoberfest). Dungeon Bowl has three catalog trophies of
// its own; BBL never awarded one, so none of these three carry a
// `tloeg.bbleague.se` id. Award files contain placement entries only
// (awardType 1/2/3) with no Best Stunty or Wooden Spoon, so no stunty/spoon
// entries are seeded for Dungeon Bowl. TP's award files have so far only
// contained team-level entries, so none of the 12 player trophies and none of
// the BBL-only cups have any TP source data to ground an id on. Those stay
// unseeded rather than carrying a guessed code -- a new TP competition
// tracking a different group, or a new award kind, would widen this set.
//
// Every trophy also records the competition group it is applicable for
// (issue #445), so the TP awards importer (tools/import-tp/src/trophy-awards/)
// can consider only applicable trophies when awarding for a competition. The
// eight unqualified "during the season" player trophies (Season MVP through
// Most SPP), plus Legendary Player and Trogen Tjänst, are curated under
// Major Season: Major is BBL's flagship season and the legend defines no
// Minor-season equivalent. Their group-scoped siblings added for issue #520
// (see the composite-id note above) carry the other groups BBL actually
// awarded them in.
// Bierhallenführer and Gudarnas Förkämpe follow their own description text,
// which is already explicit about the event they are awarded at.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
  ],
  trophies: [
